  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/... Hot temperatures will \npersist Thursday, although a gradual cooling trend will continue \nthrough the week. A weak shortwave Friday will begin the breakdown \nof an upper-level ridge, and lead to a slight chance of \nprecipitation come Friday, mainly across the higher terrain of \nsouthwest and central Idaho. Although as of now moisture looks \nrather limited. Come Sunday, guidance is in good agreement of \nanother low coming down the British Columbia coast and swing past \npast our area. This low, and associated cold front, will bring a \ncool down and increased precipitation chances (most pronounced in \nthe central ID mountains). Temperatures on Sunday will likely swing \nbelow normal following the cold frontal passage, with the lower \nSnake Plain having a 40% chance of the afternoon high being below 80 \ndegrees. Breezy conditions will persist throughout the long-term \nperiod.",
